### Use the serialized DSC property shape (1/5)

**Severity:** `medium`

The direct-execution payload must match the module's serialized settings contract. These properties use snake_case JSON names and each value is wrapped by `BoolProperty`; the current C# member names and bare booleans will not create that shape.

```suggestion
            lmb_lock_enabled = @{ value = $true }
            rmb_lock_enabled = @{ value = $true }
            mmb_lock_enabled = @{ value = $true }
```

### (6/6) Cover the no-Escape chorded release

**Severity:** `medium`

The existing lifecycle test verifies that the default release still dismisses the surfaced menu. Add a focused regression proving a caller can release all locks with dismissal disabled and the logical lock is still cleared.

```suggestion
        TEST_METHOD(ReleaseAllCanPreserveChordedClick)
        {
            FakeInjector injector;
            Engine e(injector);
            Settings s = DefaultSettings();

            e.OnButtonDown(MouseButton::Right, 0, PointL{ 0, 0 }, s);
            e.OnButtonUp(MouseButton::Right, 400, s);
            e.ReleaseAll(/*dismissContextMenu=*/false);

            Assert::IsFalse(e.IsLocked(MouseButton::Right));
            Assert::AreEqual(static_cast<size_t>(1), injector.upCalls.size());
            Assert::IsFalse(injector.upCalls[0].dismissContextMenu);
        }

        TEST_METHOD(ResetTransientClearsStaleHold)
```
